{"name":"Chervil Leaves","hex":"#abbd90","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"chervil","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A leafy herb, Anthriscus cerefolium, resembling parsley.","Leaves from the plant, used as an herb in cooking, which have a mild flavor of anise."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/chervil"},{"term":"leaves","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of leaf","from leave:\nplural of leave \nplural of leave"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of leave"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/leaves"}],"entries":[{"title":"Chervil","blocks":[{"text":"Chervil, sometimes called French parsley or garden chervil, is a delicate annual herb related to parsley. It was formerly called myrhis due to its volatile oil with an aroma similar to the resinous substance myrrh. It is commonly used to season mild-flavoured dishes and is a constituent of the French herb mixture fines herbes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/Illustration_Anthriscus_cerefolium0.jpg/330px-Illustration_Anthriscus_cerefolium0.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chervil"},{"title":"Leaf","blocks":[{"text":"A leaf is a principal appendage of the stem of a vascular plant, usually borne laterally above ground and specialized for photosynthesis. Leaves are collectively called foliage, as in \"autumn foliage\", while the leaves, stem, flower, and fruit collectively form the shoot system. In most leaves, the primary photosynthetic tissue is the palisade mesophyll and is located on the upper side of the blade or lamina of the leaf, but in some species, including the mature foliage of Eucalyptus, palisade mesophyll is present on both sides and the leaves are said to be isobilateral. The leaf is an integral part of the stem system, and most leaves are flattened and have distinct upper (adaxial) and lower (abaxial) surfaces that differ in color, hairiness, the number of stomata, the amount and structure of epicuticular wax, and other features. Leaves are mostly green in color due to the presence of a compound called chlorophyll, which is essential for photosynthesis as it absorbs light energy from the Sun. A leaf with lighter-colored or white patches or edges is called a variegated leaf."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Lisc_lipy.jpg/330px-Lisc_lipy.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg/500px-Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg/960px-Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg/500px-Farmer%27s_Market_-_Chervil_%283497853296%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFarmer's_Market_-_Chervil_(3497853296).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG/330px-Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/52/Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/52/Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG/330px-Graine_de_cerfeuil.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail",